From 79d715e975bec9383b34adb669cbb6300fcbc1de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:46:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 66/73] dockapp_prefs: Adds the dock-apps' own actions and
 preferences to their menus.

What a dock-app's menu offers is described in share/wlmaker/Dockapps.plist,
installed to the data directory: Per dock-app, 'Actions' at the top of the
menu, running a command, and a 'Preferences' submenu. A boolean preference
is an item with a check box; others are submenus with a radio button per
choice. Choices are listed in the preference, shared by name (eg. the color
themes), or read from a directory (eg. the network interfaces).

Choosing an option stores it in the dock-app's preferences file,
${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/wlmaker/<dock-app>.plist, keeping its other values, and
replacing the file atomically. The dock-app watches it, and applies the
change right away. An action's command may refer to a preference's value as
${Key}, eg. the program to open on a click; it is left out when empty.

Describes wlmcalclock, wlmcpugraph, wlmmemgraph, wlmnetgraph, wlmmixer and
wlmclock. Titles are translated to Portuguese through the i18n table.
